Source: scanbus
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jean Parpaillon <jean@parpaillon.info>
Build-Depends: cargo,
 blueprint-compiler,
 rustc,
 make,
 dpkg-dev,
 pkgconf,
 libgtk-4-dev,
 libadwaita-1-dev (>= 1.4)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0

Package: scanbus
Architecture: all
Depends: scanbus-frontend (= ${binary:Version}),
 scanbus-backend (= ${binary:Version})
Description: metapackage for the scanbus frontend and backend
 Installs both the GTK frontend and the backend components for scanbus.

Package: scanbus-frontend
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: GTK frontend for scanbus
 The graphical scanbus application for browsing scanners and launching scans.

Package: scanbus-backend
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, sane-utils
Suggests: hplip-gui
Description: scanbus D-Bus service and command-line client
 A session-scoped D-Bus service for document scanners, installed with its
 user-level systemd unit, D-Bus activation file and stable scanimage helper.
 .
 The HP backend needs hplip-gui: it owns /usr/bin/hp-systray, the only process
 that claims com.hplip.StatusService, which is where HPLIP walk-up scan events
 arrive. It is suggested rather than depended on because the Brother and mobile
 backends do not need HPLIP at all.
